s obviously  number one priority right now is we are  trying to search and rescue search and  rescue Andre says the goal here in the  Bahamas is to give the local government  less problems to solve that's what we're  trying to do to create the system of  feeding so this problem goes away and  they can take care of everything else  you are looking live at a United States  Coast Guard helicopter that is preparing  to take off it is loaded with members of  the Bahamian National Guard I talked to  one of the commanders who said the Coast  Guard is taking these Guardsmen to the  Abaco Islands I said what is their  mission is it security and she said as  she walked away rescue rescue rescue  rescue they are still in a rescue mode  right now as it pertains to the chef  it's incredible to see the resources  that he himself has brought in in order  to distribute the food he said David I  can't be tying up resources like the US  Coast Guard are begging other people who  need to actually get in and rescue folks  I need to bring in my own resources  that's why he's hired those ships and  boats and helicopters he said another  thing Tony that I'll never forget he  said when you come into a disaster zone  like this you got to have empathy and a  will to just get it done  yeah ham and cheese sandwiches to  seaplanes an amphibious vehicle what is  he expecting to encounter once he's out  there  look I mean first of all just getting to  that area finding a place to land as a  challenge but I remember last night and  that meeting that we were in Tony was so  intense right with his people at the  table and at one point he said listen  don't give me any of that fancy food we  send to restaurants that are that are  watered down or something this is not a  fancy restaurant give me the hearty  stuff that I can feed people who may not  eat another meal for two or three days  after we encountered them yeah make the  rescue and then have the good the good  stuff for the celebration David beg